        "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Mānuka」の節「Cultivation」",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M%C4%81nuka#Cultivation",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
        "revision": 1370786526,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "Numerous cultivars have been developed for garden use, of which the following have gained the Royal Horticultural Society's Award of Garden Merit: \n\n(Nanum Group) 'Kiwi'\n'Nichollsii Nanum'\n'Red Damask'\n'Silver Sheen'\nMany more cultivars are available in New Zealand but often the plant performs better in cultivation overseas. This is because in its homeland it is subject to attack by scale insects that secrete a honeydew on which grows a sooty mould that eventually debilitates the plant. Because of this, attempts have been made, with limited commercial success, to cross the showy New Zealand cultivars with mould-resistant Australian Leptospermum species.",
        "truncated": false
      }
